\section{Backend Implementation Summary (Laravel E-Commerce System)}

\subsection{1. Order Processing System}
The order system implements a fully transactional checkout pipeline ensuring data integrity and consistency.

\begin{itemize}
    \item Cart validation prior to checkout execution
    \item Stock validation with race-condition prevention using \texttt{lockForUpdate()}
    \item Atomic order creation using database transactions
    \item Conversion of cart items into order items
    \item Stock decrement after successful purchase
    \item Cart cleanup after order completion
    \item Order cancellation with stock restoration
    \item Email notifications via queued \texttt{OrderConfirmed} mailable
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Key Improvements:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Prevented overselling using row-level locking
    \item Ensured price consistency using locked product references
    \item Full rollback safety using database transactions
\end{itemize}

\subsection{2. User Profile and Address Management}
The user system supports multi-model persistence combining user identity and physical address management.

\begin{itemize}
    \item User profile updates (name, email)
    \item Address management using \texttt{updateOrCreate()}
    \item Guaranteed single primary address per user
\end{itemize}

This ensures automatic creation or update of user addresses while maintaining data consistency.
\subsection{3. API Layer (Laravel Sanctum)}
A RESTful API layer was implemented following JSON-API principles to support external and mobile consumption.

\begin{itemize}
    \item Public catalog endpoint: \texttt{GET /api/catalog}
    \item Authenticated user endpoint: \texttt{GET /api/user}
    \item Product relationships loaded via eager loading (category, images)
    \item Authentication secured using Laravel Sanctum with Bearer Token support
\end{itemize}

\subsection{4. Administrative \& Support UI Overhaul}
\textit{Objective: Ensure all system touchpoints, including back-office and support, meet luxury standards.}

